# SimuCell3D 2.0 documentation (archived)

:::{important}
These pages are the documentation of release 2.0, re-rendered as it was written. They have not
been updated, and some of their statements are wrong (see the corrections below). For the current
release, read the **[current documentation]({{SITE}}stable/)**.
:::

## This release

Release
: SimuCell3D 2.0, 2 March 2026, the first maintenance release after 1.0

Maintainer
: Nilesh Patil, on a fork: [github.com/nilesh-patil/simucell3d](https://github.com/nilesh-patil/simucell3d)

Tag
: `v2.0`, commit `343bd98`

SimuCell3D
: created by Steve Runser, Roman Vetter and Dagmar Iber (Iber Lab, ETH Zurich); article [doi:10.1038/s43588-024-00620-9](https://doi.org/10.1038/s43588-024-00620-9)

SimuCell3D was created by Steve Runser, Roman Vetter and Dagmar Iber (Iber Lab, ETH Zurich). The
2.x releases are maintained by Nilesh Patil on a fork and are not reviewed or endorsed by the
authors.

The pages below are the Markdown documentation in tag `v2.0`: the `README.md`, the `doc/`
folder, the README files of `examples/`, `scripts/`, `src/mesh/` and `baselines/`, and the
plans in `docs/plans/`. The root files `INSTALL.md`, `GETTING_STARTED.md`, `FAQ.md` and
`CONTRIBUTING.md` are symbolic links to pages of `doc/getting-started/` and are not repeated. The
tag also contains two PDF copies of the article and its supplement (`doc/SimuCell3D.pdf`,
`doc/SimuCell3D-extra.pdf`); they are not published here, and links to them go to the article's
DOI. The [release notes of 2.0]({{SITE}}stable/whats_new/v2.0.html)
summarise the changes from 1.0.

## Corrections

:::{warning}
**Read this before you rely on these pages.** The following was found after the release. The
original text below is left as it was.

- **Citation.** The README cites the article as "Runser, Adrien and others". The correct
  citation is: Runser, S., Vetter, R. & Iber, D. SimuCell3D: three-dimensional simulation of
  tissue mechanics with cell polarization. *Nat. Comput. Sci.* **4**, 299-309 (2024).
  [doi:10.1038/s43588-024-00620-9](https://doi.org/10.1038/s43588-024-00620-9).
- **"Full backward compatibility", "no new scientific features", "all v1.0 commands work without
  modification".** These statements are wrong. 2.0 changes simulation results compared with 1.0,
  because it fixes the contact distance to a face interior and the time integration of contact
  model 2.
  The parameter files moved from the repository root to `parameters/`, and the lab's growth
  benchmark file of 1.0, `parameters_benchmarck.xml`, was removed without a note. Do not use 2.0
  to reproduce the published figures; use 1.0 (the Zenodo archive
  [doi:10.5281/zenodo.10796908](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10796908) cited by the article).
- **Build badge.** The "build passing" badge in the README was a static image, not live CI status.
- **Growth runs fail early.** In the November 2026 benchmark (8-core cloud machines), no 2.0
  run of the lab's growth benchmark grew past 216 cells, and the shipped long monolayer vesicle
  file crashed. See
  [which cases complete]({{SITE}}stable/benchmarks/completion.html)
  in the current documentation.
- **Licence file.** The `LICENSE` file of 2.0 added a copyright line that release 1.0 does not
  have. Release 2.1.0 restored the licence text of 1.0 and states the authorship in `NOTICE`
  (see [licence and notice](licence.md)).

These corrections are also recorded in the
[GitHub release notes of 2.0](https://github.com/nilesh-patil/simucell3d/releases/tag/v2.0) and in
the [changelog](https://github.com/nilesh-patil/simucell3d/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).
:::

## Obtaining and building 2.0

```console
$ git clone https://github.com/nilesh-patil/simucell3d.git
$ cd simucell3d
$ git checkout v2.0
$ mkdir build
$ cd build
$ cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release ..
$ make -j4
$ ./simucell3d ../parameters/core/parameters_vesicle.xml
```

Release 2.0 needs a C++17 compiler with OpenMP and CMake. Like 1.0 it declares
`cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.0)`, which CMake 4 refuses; with CMake 4, add
`-DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5` to the `cmake` line. The quick-start page of 2.0 says
`cd SimuCell3D` after the clone; the clone creates the directory `simucell3d`. The option
`--version` does not exist in 2.0.

